{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 4 'D417|ladderable|ladder' docs/DECISIONS.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html | head -160\"","aggregated_output":"docs/DECISIONS.md-171-\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-172-## 7. Thesis library (PRD 06)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-173-\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-174-**Questions**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:175:- A question is one question with a fixed ladder and a due date, never rewritten: five checkable, non-overlapping rungs covering every\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-176-  outcome (an asset question strongly bullish to strongly bearish for the business, a theme question named by outcome), two for a yes/no\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-177-  question (D38, D46; the outcome rungs against guidance of D186 come with the next extraction version, §6).\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-178-- A number question names its period; a company's figures use its fiscal year; at most this year and next open (D46, D248 boundary 4).\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-179-- Any company's own quantity is a thesis under that company, private companies included (D187); *(not built; to be built, D368: it needs\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-379-| D34 | 2026-10-18 | An SEC filing is dated by the day SEC makes it public | in force | §1 System |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-380-| D35 | 2026-10-18 | Extraction v1 is final | superseded by D37, D274 | Extraction |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-381-| D36 | 2026-10-18 | One word per concept in the input and extraction modules | in force (amended by D41, D47, D52, D54, D57, D163) | §15 Working rules |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-382-| D37 | 2026-10-18 | Freeze v1 of the input side and extraction | in force (amended by D41, D51, D58, D59) | §1 System |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:383:| D38 | 2026-10-20 | The views database rebuilt: a view is a question with a five-rung ladder and a due date | in force (amended by D42, D45, D46, D51, D54, D57, D58, D185, D186, D198, D260) | §7 Thesis library |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-384-| D39 | 2026-10-20 | Writing into the views database: match by where a candidate belongs, then one round of re-judging | in force (amended by D42, D44, D45, D46, D51, D63, D155, D169, D202, D204) | §7 Thesis library |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-385-| D40 | 2026-10-20 | The matching judge: a general model first, every match recorded, humans label, a small model later | in force (amended by D42, D44, D45, D46, D169, D190) | §7 Thesis library |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-386-| D41 | 2026-10-20 | What the rebuilt views database changes outside it | in force (amended by D42, D45, D51, D54, D190, D191, D195, D356, D374) | §4 Config |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-387-| D42 | 2026-10-20 | Extraction hands over evidence and candidate views as two things; evidence is matched to what its view alre… | in force (amended by D45, D58, D59, D198, D202, D204, D207, D264, D360, D364) | §6 Extraction |\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-676-| D332 | 2026-10-27 | Use a pulsing black Monitoring dot | in force | [frontend](DECISIONS-frontend.md) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-677-| D333 | 2026-10-27 | Default the Action chart to one year | in force | [frontend](DECISIONS-frontend.md) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-678-| D334 | 2026-10-27 | Clean up frontend component ownership | record | Frontend |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-679-| D335 | 2026-10-30 | Each adopted thesis offers only its own two endpoints; two-rung cards show their own Yes/No | in force | §12 Idea API and service |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:680:| D336 | 2026-10-30 | A yes/no ladder with named outcomes shows its outcome once | in force | [frontend](DECISIONS-frontend.md) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-681-| D337 | 2026-10-27 | Create the Singapore Lightsail development server | record | Operations |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-682-| D338 | 2026-10-27 | Test single-call extraction stability by correcting the task and preserving the request | in force | §6 Extraction |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-683-| D339 | 2026-10-27 | Measure a source/route extraction POC against Luna and DeepSeek | record | Extraction |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-684-| D340 | 2026-10-27 | Specify the source stage and research routing/admission before more model runs | record | Extraction |\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-736-| D392 | 2026-11-09 | Seeded end-to-end diagnostic of the clean system: the 22 seeds as a measurement-only fixture, a same-day v108 control via a separate harness, Stages 0–2 approved (Stage 2 runs if Stage 1 meets its frozen line) | in force | round log §60; council/en-claude.md |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-737-| D393 | 2026-11-09 | After Stage 2 of D392 (clean +5, inconclusive on q12), fix capital spending (q12) first; c8 may change for it as a new version measured against c8; the unseeded measurement waits | in force | `clean-arch/q12-capex-2026-11-09/DESIGN.md`; round log §63 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-738-| D394 | 2026-11-10 | Capital spending (q12) is a known gap after arms c12 and c13 failed (the model does not recall the cash-flow identity unprompted); c8 stays; the unseeded measurement starts with its $0 question-matching stage, an addition to the measurement, with the paid draw on Alex's word | in force | round log §§64–65 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-739-| D395 | 2026-11-10 | Run the unseeded clean measurement: three draws from an empty library, opened questions matched by the frozen rule (MATCHING-v2) through an independent reading, graded on q04, q05, q08, q09, q13, q18 and q23, every other question reported | in force | `clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/MATCHING-v2.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:740:| D396 | 2026-11-10 | Design the clean system's own judging step (Step 4): ladders and judgements for its own questions; first test is independent readers checking its answers against the sources; design and council before any code or paid send | in force | round log §67 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:741:| D397 | 2026-11-10 | Clean Step 4's ladder step: a topic that asks more than one thing gets one judged question (the part its outcome names); the other parts are shown as not judged; a departure from D38 for topics with two real bets, recorded as an open defect | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §4 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:742:| D398 | 2026-11-10 | Clean Step 4's ladder step carries D186 in full: ranges stated against the reference (D260's list), the favourable end registered with its reason, rungs ordered and labelled by code; a number question with no reference is marked so | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §4 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:743:| D399 | 2026-11-10 | The clean ladder request may teach how to build an event's five states (outcomes that exclude one another, one or two divided by a property that holds or does not), with a general example | superseded by D409 | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:744:| D400 | 2026-11-10 | Stage A of the clean ladder step is read against Alex's absolute lines with no paid control arm (an exception to AGENTS §7.3 for this first measurement); the lines are fixed; every report says it does not compare with production | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:745:| D401 | 2026-11-10 | Once a fresh review finds nothing serious, the ladder step is built and Stage A sent without asking again, capped at $3; a missed line stops and goes to Alex; Stage B needs his word again | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:746:| D402 | 2026-11-10 | Before more review or the build, the clean ladder step's request is sent once on six stored theses for a few cents, and the answers read by hand and reported to Alex; what follows is his to choose; D401's conditions stand | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:747:| D403 | 2026-11-10 | On the clean ladder step an event's due day is a date the thesis or the article gives, or the last day of the thesis's period; the model picks no other day (narrower than v74i line 26, by Alex's decision) | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §4 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:748:| D404 | 2026-11-10 | After the six-request probe: the model is asked which instruction led to each fault, the request is changed for the probe's three classes and a theme's state names may not be the company's labels, the same six are sent once more, and when the classes are gone the ladder step is built and Stage A sent on D401's terms with no further design-review round; if not gone, back to Alex | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:749:| D405 | 2026-11-10 | The clean ladder step accepts a reference's words only as an unbroken passage of the article (spacing, case and quote-mark forms aside); otherwise the answer is refused and sent back once, and a second refusal writes no question | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.3, check 6 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:750:| D406 | 2026-11-10 | On the clean ladder step the decision to decline and the naming of a theme's states move from sentences into the answer's shape (first fields: what the topic's outcome names and which is the main one; separate shapes for a company's and a theme's states); then eight stored theses are sent three times each and read as counts; when steady, the build follows on D401's terms | in force; its first point (the fields naming the main thing) superseded by D407 | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:751:| D407 | 2026-11-10 | One last probe of the clean ladder request (the first request plus the exact-copy and stand-alone sentences and separate shapes for company and theme states; eight theses, three sends, beside the first request as control), then the build whichever way it comes out: met (no-main topics declined 8 of 9, the others answered 15 of 15) the build uses it; missed, the first request unchanged with the faults of writing refused by code | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:752:| D408 | 2026-11-10 | Stage A of the clean ladder step missed its lines: the work stays at the step; the event answers are changed first, checked at no cost and reviewed, then the same Stage A is run once more within D401's $3; the other classes follow one at a time; Stage B is not started | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/result/RESULT.md`; `DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:753:| D409 | 2026-11-10 | On the clean ladder step an event is answered in at most three outcomes: it has happened by the due day, it is ruled out, or neither, the third written by code; finer differences are listed as not judged | in force; supersedes D399 | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:754:| D410 | 2026-11-10 | A group named in a judged question as the trade names it (\"the big four AI hyperscalers\") and not listed member by member is not a fault of the question (mark Q of the Stage A form) | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/stage-a-reader-brief.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-755-| D411 | 2026-11-10 | A figure's reference may be the amount last reported when the article states no expectation, named as that and never as the market's expectation; a reference stated as a range is carried as a range; built and measured after the event answers | in force; built and probed, not yet measured | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2.2 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-756-| D412 | 2026-11-10 | Every round is reflected on in the council to a recorded consensus, then the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals; every trace is read by Claude itself | in force | AGENTS §7.3; round log §69 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-757-| D413 | 2026-11-10 | Where neither the topic nor the item settles it, an amount the company owes, guarantees or has committed to pay is registered with the lower end favourable; a topic that says more is good keeps \"higher\"; a tie rule in the request, the decision stays the model's | in force; built, measured in the third Stage A | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2.4 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-758-| D414 | 2026-11-10 | Code sets the due day of a year's figure whose day would be an estimate: the fiscal year-end plus 60 days for the company, the calendar year-end plus 90 for a theme; a stated day is kept; a figure that is not a year's is dealt with first, apart | in force; built, measured in the third Stage A | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2.4 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:759:| D415 | 2026-11-10 | The third Stage A of the clean ladder step is sent without asking again once each change (D413, D414, the scope of a ruling out, D411) is proved small and reviewed; a change that does not pass stops and goes to Alex; Stage B needs his word | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-760-| D416 | 2026-11-10 | Alex's six lines stay; the ruling out of an event is tried as a typed answer (who decides, what they decide) and proved small on the six product-deadline theses beside the present shape before anything else | in force; passed its second trial alone, in the working request, measured in the fourth Stage A | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2.5 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:761:| D417 | 2026-11-10 | A figure for a period that is not one year (a rolling twelve months) with no publication day in the texts is declined, with that reason | in force; proved small, in the working request | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2.5; mark N of the Stage A form |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-762-| D418 | 2026-11-10 | A government's or regulator's permission, restriction or ban on a class of products or trade belongs to the theme that covers it, also for the company's own product; a proceeding against the company itself stays the company's | in force; narrowed, passed alone, in the working request | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2.5; mark O of the Stage A form |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:763:| D419 | 2026-11-10 | The fourth Stage A is sent without asking again once each change (D416, D417, D418) is proved small and reviewed; a change that does not pass stops and goes to Alex; Stage B needs his word | superseded by D421 for these changes | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-764-| D420 | 2026-11-10 | A proceeding an authority conducts: a published closing decision is the event happened; its formal abandonment or withdrawal without the asked-for conclusion is the event ruled out; its still going on is the wait; such an event always has a ruling out; the question stays the one the thesis names | in force; passed alone, in the working request | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5.2.5; mark R of the Stage A form |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:765:| D421 | 2026-11-10 | D417 into the working request; then D420's rule, D418's narrowed sentence and the typed ruling out are each tested alone and reviewed; all passing, the fourth Stage A is sent without asking again; one failing stops and goes to Alex | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-766-| D422 | 2026-11-10 | A second look by the model at its own answer (one more call, one instruction that names no fault) is tested small on 66 stored answers of the fourth Stage A, as a candidate; pass and fail written beforehand; whether the step adopts it is Alex's after the result | done; not adopted (D425). Run on 76 answers (the council corrected the grouping: 18 agreed, 18 disputed, 10 held, 30 unfaulted): it did not pass (6 of the 18 mended against 9; 3 of the 30 counted against it, the page fails at 3). Adoption is Alex's and is not decided | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/probe-second-look-2026-11-10/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-767-| D423 | 2026-11-10 | Work on Jev's revision relation stops (open defect); \"a later version does not take the older record's questions\" accepted as a direction, measured by the council and withdrawn by its author: the writer's rule stays, pending Alex's word | in force for the stop; the rule settled by D424 | `clean-arch/step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/LOG.md`; Step 2 log §§15–16 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-768-| D424 | 2026-11-10 | The clean writer keeps giving a \"later version\" the older record's questions (D202's rule); removing it is closed without a change; the carried context links are a recorded defect; \"a company's answer sits wherever its report is filed\" is not decided | in force | `clean-arch/step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/LOG.md` §6; Step 2 log §16 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:769:| D425 | 2026-11-10 | The ladder step takes no second look: the test (D422) did not pass; the step stays as it ran in the fourth Stage A | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/probe-second-look-2026-11-10/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:770:| D426 | 2026-11-10 | The ladder step is not tuned further on the 44 theses and no fifth Stage A is sent; Stage A has not passed (lines 1, 3, 4 missed by 1 to 3 answers of 131); by his word the preparation of Stage B opens on that step, its $0 baseline reading of the 159 stored judgements first; no paid Stage B send without his word again | in force (an exception to D401's stop at a missed line) | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-771-| D427 | 2026-11-11 | Clean Step 2 (search, Jev comparison, best-match grouping, forward runner, Step 3 library) closed and frozen; not moved into production alone; goes to production with the whole clean path after Step 4 meets its lines, through an end-to-end comparison against production on the frozen ruler (three draws each) | in force | `tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py`; clean-arch PRD §5; Step 2 log §19 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-772-| D428 | 2026-11-11 | Stage B's lines: decided figure-question judgements UNSUPPORTED at most 5 points above the baseline's (12.7% to 14.4%), yes/no at most 5%, last judgements at most 3 in 30 UNSUPPORTED with INSUFFICIENT beside; no overall line | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:773:| D429 | 2026-11-11 | Build the adapter's ladder mode ($0, tests, mutants, fresh reviews until one finds nothing serious), then send Stage B's three draws without asking again (cap $2), read each judgement alone with the baseline's form, controls and count | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §5, §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-774-| D430 | 2026-11-12 | Stage B line 3: a figure control's due day counts as the ruler's when both mark the same period's publication; an event's deadline must be the ruler's; the literal reading counted beside | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/STAGE_B_READING.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-775-| D431 | 2026-11-12 | D427's end-to-end comparison is against production as it now runs (no preset questions, D370), frozen ruler, same day, three draws each; the seven graded questions beside; the seeded comparison stays a diagnostic | in force | `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/kr-consensus.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:776:| D432 | 2026-11-12 | After Stage B: diagnose how Step 1 cuts a matter into theses (the nine unopened graded questions, the eight theses with no ladder, the remaining Stage A faults); the diagnosis and one change, as a new Step 1 version measured on fresh articles, go to Alex before any build | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/PROGRESS-2026-11-12.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-777-| D433 | 2026-11-12 | Open Step 1 candidate c14: D38's year boundary carried into two merge sentences (+151 characters); first a small probe of c8 and c14 on stored articles with fixed stop lines; prompt audit and council before its first send; c8 stays in force until c14 is shown better on fresh articles | in force | `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/DIAGNOSIS.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-778-| D434 | 2026-11-13 | c14 stopped (stage 1: 7 of 9 against 8), c8 stays; diagnose the second-thing shapes at $0, then combine the year boundary, the customer-spending collision and that class, each shown small on stored data, into one Step 1 version measured once against c8 on fresh articles; the plan goes to Alex first | in force | `c