swers for Stage B; two gates of fresh-input checks (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/READING-PLAN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-797-| D453 | 2026-11-13 | Redo c2's Step 1 from empty after a dropped response at item 56 (an eligible transport failure under D449); no ceiling change (council consensus, D439) | in force | `poc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/c2/run.json` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-798-| D454 | 2026-11-13 | Full run read so far: census clean ≈ production, every loss at opening; Stage A missed on fresh theses; readings continue: loss-trace marks, then Stage B (gate 2), then a reflection on question scope and deadline (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/CENSUS-FULL-RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-799-| D455 | 2026-11-13 | Full run: Stage B line 3 unexercised under every treatment (0 settled, at most 4 controls with material shown); the judgement reading stops (a recorded departure from D452/D454); next the reflection on question scope and deadline (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/CENSUS-FULL-RESULT.md` |\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-806-| D462 | 2026-11-13 | F6 (the shared-quantity date sentence) recorded as a contradiction with uncertain standalone effect (decisive in 1–2 of 26 declines); status report for Alex first, then the $0 identity comparison (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/step1-audit/f6/` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-807-| D463 | 2026-11-13 | Identity lever: a general clause in clean Step 1 first (candidate c16), written with narrowed boundaries and two or three general examples per class, and a frozen fresh-article probe, both reviewed before any send (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/step1-audit/IDENTITY-COMPARISON.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-808-| D464 | 2026-11-13 | Send the case-specific identity diagnostic (c16 v5 against c8; one fresh story per target, 7 merge and 9 negative stories, stored guards), 258 jobs under one $5 ledger; result goes back to the council, never to adoption (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/identity-probe/v2/PROBE-DESIGN-v2.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-809-| D465 | 2026-11-13 | Identity diagnostic: the year boundary moved its error (2026 swapped for 2027); line stopped, c16 not adopted, c8 stays; Ohio clause and F6 kept as leads (council consensus) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/identity-probe/v2/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:810:| D466 | 2026-11-13 | Deep reflection: stop circling; two choices for Alex (a real prior research library or an empty start; the three open shapes as targets or concerns); the clean ladder step measured on the same questions and facts, prepared at $0, sent only on his word; new guard lines proposed (council consensus) | in force | `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-2.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:811:| D467 | 2026-11-13 | Ladder-cost measurement: feasible only with four more $0 proofs and a same-day control; it changes no final answer by itself, so it goes to Alex as a candidate beside the two pending choices (council consensus) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/ladder-cost/FEASIBILITY.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:812:| D468 | 2026-11-13 | Ladder-cost measurement stops at its $0 proofs (control rebuild, ladder swap, blind-chosen case articles kept as tools); forward work waits on Alex's two D466 choices; the measurement offered as an option (council consensus) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/ladder-cost/` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:813:| D469 | 2026-11-13 | Provisional (Alex not answering, D439): empty-start measurement; the three open shapes stay concerns; the ladder-step refusal fix starts with a $0 boundary check of every \"no main\" refusal (council consensus) | in force | `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-6.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:814:| D470 | 2026-11-13 | Ladder-refusal candidate stopped (readers split on the boundary); 41 Stage A splits recorded, eight read provisionally by D414; Stage A verdict unchanged; the written-ladder line question opened for the council (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/stage-a-splits/splits.json` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:815:| D471 | 2026-11-13 | Written-ladder line kept; ten right-by-refusal theses traced (period rule read as a horizon in three); c17 (period sentence clarified) probed on stored cases under frozen lines (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/period-probe/PERIOD-PROBE-DESIGN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-816-| D472 | 2026-11-13 | Period probe budget exception: the nine never-sent jobs sent alone under a $0.50 ceiling before any answer is read; the timed-out send stays missing (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-14.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-817-| D473 | 2026-11-13 | Period candidate c17 fails (target 0 of 3; memory-price theses 10 → 3, federal 3 → 0); not adopted; Step 1 sentence changes on these articles stop (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/period-probe/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-818-| D474 | 2026-11-13 | Unsigned-deal candidate c18 (D388 at the binding-obligation definition) probed on unseen articles against the acceptance library: one target story, six negatives, guards (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/unsigned-deals/PROBE-DESIGN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-819-| D475 | 2026-11-13 | c18 not adopted (unseen target not moved: 4 of 6 against c8 3 of 6; no regression; Ohio 6 of 9 against 0); D473 federal line within c8 variance (correction note) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/unsigned-deals/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:820:| D476 | 2026-11-13 | Ladder-cost comparison not sent; next: a $0 two-reader source check of the eleven first-pass refusals (worth asking apart from can be laddered), no automatic threshold (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/reachability/` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-821-\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-192-  on time, gets its \"now\" as an input (D14, D54).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-193-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-194-## D13 · 2026-10-16 · The system is driven by information, not by the calendar\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-195-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:196:- By: Alex (\"时间是一直往前推进，但是增额推荐是现实的时间，你抽取出来未来会成为thesis 或是ladder, evidence 的东西是会被这些\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-197-  streming events 影响的，不是按照每一天来的 … 不需要按部就班的推日期，有相关的信息抽取出现，自然会影响整个系统抽取的thesis\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-198-  向前\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-199-- Decides: the system moves forward only when an item arrives. Its facts are attached to objects, and the theses,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:200:  ladders and evidence that depend on those objects move forward from them. There is no daily step anywhere in the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:201:  system, including the layers not designed yet; a day without items changes nothing. Later designs (thesis, ladder,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-202-  evidence) are built on this.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-203-- Enforced: the summary and the store node of `docs/system-design/new-design.js`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-204-- Scope (D14): this is the stream mode. Date- or schedule-triggered work exists only in the pull mode.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-205-\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-207-\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-208-- By: Alex (\"下面肯定会探讨到例如thesis 里面的laddar /evidence 有些可能到期日就需要看下证据或是甚至主动的run 一个cron 来看下是否\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-209-  满足。这是stream的相反模式，也就是pull mode (agent 主动查找）这个我们后面设计，但是我希望你分的很清楚这两种模式\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-210-- Decides: the system has two modes. Stream mode (designed now): items arrive and their facts move dependent theses,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:211:  ladders and evidence forward; it never reads the calendar (D13). Pull mode (designed later): at a ladder's or an\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-212-  evidence's due date, or on a cron schedule, an agent in the system actively looks for evidence and checks whether a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-213-  condition is met; it is the only place where time triggers work. \"Pull\" names only this agent-initiated checking;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-214-  the upstream pipeline that feeds the stream is called upstream supply, not pull.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-215-- Enforced: the summary, the thesis and pull nodes and the overview view of `docs/system-design/new-design.js`.\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-439-  it needs; financial-report lines are evidence, never its definition. Reading every reported number as it streams\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-440-  in builds a store the theses then search, and lets the available numbers shape the theses. The old system's stored\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-441-  data shows it: for three companies it kept 11,841 numbers, of which the theses cited 543 (4.6%); of the 21 KPIs the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-442-  theses watched, 9 appear in no table at all and none of those 9 got a number.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:443:- Decides: financial reports are not part of the stream. When a thesis's ladder or evidence needs a number from a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-444-  report (for example \"if Apple's iPhone revenue turns negative year over year next quarter, the view fails\"), pull\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-445-  mode fetches that number at the due date and checks it. Stream mode keeps the items that move theses as they arrive.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:446:  The research conclusions (thesis, ladder, evidence) are designed next; extraction and the research store follow\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-447-  from what a thesis needs (the fact-path drafts of D23 are paused, not deleted: a number's identity and \"the same\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-448-  value again is a confirmation\" may be reused).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-449-- Differs from the old system: the old system fetched each company's whole financial statements on every refresh\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-450-  (provider statements plus the tables of every 10-Q/10-K), kept every line and its derived growth, and offered the\n--\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-505-  什么这些是客观的信息，你的模型抽取出来的东西才是真的\"; \"这个观点其实也是因子，只是他可能是一系列量化+非量化的evidence来支撑的\";\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-506-  on closing: \"一个thesis 如果被证伪了，应该被invalidate, 或是过期了，被invalidate, 但是应该存在这个db里面以供历史查询\"; on\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-507-  levels: \"我觉得分开。之前也说过宏观类型的thesis 其实是公司层次之外的\"; on drivers: \"前者，need be specific\"; on sources:\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-508-  \"你的观点抽取一定要附带这个观点的source 是哪里来的，这样可以未来快速查找文件/数据源来做reason\"; and \"1. 这个没问题\" to the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:509:  views database being thesis · ladder · evidence).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:510:- Decides: the system builds, updates and closes a views database; it is the thesis · ladder · evidence of the design\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-511-  page, and the research store merges into it (the store's paused draft of number identities and observations is\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-512-  dropped; processing records stay). Structure: object (company, crypto, commodity, theme, all from the universe) →\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-513-  driver (specific: who does what to what; its definition is never rewritten, a change is a new driver with a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-514-  redirect) → view. A view has a one-sentence claim that is never rewritten (a change is a new view that supersedes\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-515-  it), a direction (up or down), a horizon class (short or long) with a due date, for object views a stance on the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:516:  object, a rationale that cites evidence, an optional premise, confirm and falsify conditions (the ladder), evidence,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-517-  a status (active, confirmed, falsified, expired, merged, superseded, no longer tracked) and versions. Views are the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-518-  model's judgments; evidence is objective (who said what, where). Two levels: theme views say what will happen in the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md-519-  world; object views say what will happen to the object, and name a theme view (or another object's view) as their\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
